          "content": "Start each study with a labeled sketch of the particle, film, interface, surrounding medium and physically relevant transport or electronic pathways. Specify particle geometry, whether it is dispersed or supported, and whether the observation is a bulk, surface, optical or colloidal signal. Predict limiting behavior of every equation and identify its valid parameter range before entering numbers. For numerical exercises, report input units, intermediate quantities, numerical precision and a reasonableness check. The two model cards in each unit are simple independent controls, not coupled predictions of a fabricated device. The capstone demands a falsifiable physical explanation and a feasible characterization plan.",
